From 8d6b625ffb482cbc81bfdb2d539e680b7c5123f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:44:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Parse BSS Load IE to fix Channel Scan Report
 Utilization Present

translate_nl_data_to_bwl_results() parses NL80211_BSS_INFORMATION_ELEMENTS
from the kernel's scan-cache entry to populate sChannelScanResults for the
1905 Channel Scan Report, but its IE-parsing switch only handled SSID (0),
HT Operation (61), and VHT Operation (192). The BSS Load Information
Element (ID 11, 802.11-2020 9.4.2.28) -- the element that actually carries
per-neighbor Station Count and Channel Utilization -- was never parsed.

As a result, sChannelScanResults::load_bss_ie_present stayed at its
zero-initialized default for every neighbor, so
channel_scan_task.cpp::set_neighbor_in_scan_results_tlv() always took the
"FIELD_NOT_PRESENT" branch when filling wfa_map::cNeighbors, and
channel_utilization / station_count were never written to the wire. In
Wireshark this showed up as "Neighbor Flags: 0x00, Utilization Present:
False" for every neighbor in the Channel Scan Report, even when the
scanned AP was advertising real BSS Load data in its beacons -- confirmed
against a working reference capture that showed
"Neighbor Flags: 0x80, Utilization Present: True" with a non-zero
Channel Utilization for the same scenario.

Add a case for BSS Load IE (11) to the IE-parsing loop:
  - Station Count               : 2 bytes, little-endian
  - Channel Utilization         : 1 byte
  - Available Admission Capacity: 2 bytes, little-endian (unused)

and set load_bss_ie_present = 1, channel_utilization and station_count
from it, so set_neighbor_in_scan_results_tlv() now takes the
FIELD_PRESENT branch and reports the real driver-observed values.

This is a follow-up fix on top of the nl80211 Channel Scan HAL support
introduced in 0386-Channel-Scan-nl80211-Support.patch and
0387-Channel-Scan-fixes-for-parallel-scan.patch, where neighbor discovery
(BSSID/SSID/signal/channel/bandwidth) was validated but the BSS Load
(utilization/station-count) IE parsing was missed since it lives in the
same function but is an independent parsing branch.

Additionally, 802.11 BSS Load IE reports Channel Utilization as a raw byte
on a 0-255 scale (255 = 100% busy), as confirmed by matching
`iw scan dump` output on-device (e.g. "channel utilisation: 197/255").

The EasyMesh Multi-AP Channel Scan Result TLV expects this field
as a genuine percentage (0-100). Without scaling, values like 197-246
were being forwarded as-is, producing out-of-range utilization
percentages (e.g. 200%) in the 1905 Channel Scan Report seen on the
Controller/Wireshark side.

Fix: scale the raw byte by (raw * 100) / 255 before storing it in
sChannelScanResults::channel_utilization, and extend the debug log
to print both the converted percentage and the original raw byte.

Signed-off-by: Manoj Sekar <sekar@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 .../bwl/nl80211/mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp      | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp b/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
index 99961e7..a566681 100644
--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/mon_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
@@ -252,6 +252,33 @@ static bool translate_nl_data_to_bwl_results(sChannelScanResults &results,
                 }
             }
             break;
+        case 11: // BSS Load (802.11-2020 9.4.2.28)
+            // [CHAN-SCAN] This is the element that feeds the per-neighbor "Channel
+            // Utilization" / "Station Count" / "Utilization Present" fields of the
+            // EasyMesh Channel Scan Report Neighbor structure (wfa_map::cNeighbors).
+            // Without parsing it here, sChannelScanResults::load_bss_ie_present stays at
+            // its zero-initialized default, so channel_scan_task.cpp's
+            // set_neighbor_in_scan_results_tlv() always takes the "FIELD_NOT_PRESENT"
+            // branch and Wireshark shows "Neighbor Flags: 0x00, Utilization Present: False"
+            // for every neighbor, even though the driver/AP is advertising real BSS Load
+            // data in its beacons.
+            //   Station Count               : 2 bytes, little-endian
+            //   Channel Utilization         : 1 byte
+            //   Available Admission Capacity: 2 bytes, little-endian (not used here)
+            if (len >= 5) {
+                results.station_count =
+                    static_cast<uint16_t>(data[0] | (static_cast<uint16_t>(data[1]) << 8));
+                results.channel_utilization = (static_cast<uint32_t>(data[2]) * 100) / 255;
+                results.load_bss_ie_present = 1;
+                LOG(DEBUG) << "[CHAN-SCAN] BSS Load IE parsed for " << results.bssid
+                           << ": station_count=" << results.station_count
+                           << " channel_utilization=" << int(results.channel_utilization)
+                           << "% (raw=" << int(data[2]) << ")";
+            } else {
+                LOG(DEBUG) << "[CHAN-SCAN] BSS Load IE present but too short (len=" << len
+                           << ") for " << results.bssid << " - ignoring";
+            }
+            break;
         default:
             break;
         }
-- 
